message: If you use this reproducibility artifact, please cite the artifact and the associated manuscript.
title: 'Carbon-Water Trade-offs in Geo-distributed AI Inference Allocation under Water-Stress Screening: Reproducibility Artifact'
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-23
repository-code: https://github.com/hisnghkkbfuu/geo-ai-carbon-water-allocation-artifact
license: MIT
type: software
abstract: >-
  Independent reproducibility artifact for a scenario-bounded, trace-driven
  lexicographic allocation analysis. The package contains portable code,
  author-created derived inputs and results, figure source data, frozen exports,
  and deterministic tests. It does not redistribute third-party raw request
  traces or claim measured operator outcomes.
keywords:
  - AI inference
  - geo-distributed data centers
  - carbon-aware scheduling
  - workload migration
  - direct water use
  - water stress
  - lexicographic optimization
